  ('balandra-beach-mexico', '10S', 'Balandra Beach (Playa Balandra)', 'Mexico', 'Balandra beach La Paz', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Baja California Sur (Los Cabos & La Paz)', '{"tropical","family","romance"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["CONANP Natural Protected Area since 2008; ~25 km north of La Paz","Two fixed daily shifts (08:00-12:00 / 13:00-17:00), ~450 visitors per slot, first-come","Conservation bracelet required ~MXN 125 pp/day (under-12s, seniors/retirees, disabilities exempt with ID)","No commercial food service inside the bay; limited services (toilets/info) - bring own water/shade/snacks","El Hongo mushroom rock is the emblem of Balandra and La Paz; shallow calm turquoise water"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"limited on-site (toilets/info only); serious cases ~25 km to La Paz - Hospital Salvatierra/ISSSTE/private + air-evac; carry medical insurance","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"effectively none in Baja California Sur","dengue":"circulates in Mexico - use repellent","water":"carry own bottled/purified water - no services in the bay","hurricane":"Jun-Nov - trip insurance for summer/fall","day_use":"TIMED-ENTRY two shifts + ~450/slot cap, first-come, arrive >=30 min early; CONANP bracelet required; NO food vendors inside","sun_heat":"scarce shade - umbrella, hat, reef-safe sunscreen, ample water","el_hongo":"protected/restored rock - do not climb or touch","swimming":"shallow, calm, family-safe but NO lifeguards - supervise children, watch outgoing tide; no diving (wading/kayak beach)","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Apr (dry desert winter, comfortable) - slot cap fills fastest, arrive early; rides La Paz high season","shoulder":"May & Sep-Oct (warm, quieter slots, easier entry)","green":"Jun-Aug (summer heat + hurricane window, scarce shade - early-slot only; domestic holidays spike)","booking_window_lead_time":"no lodging to pre-book; conservation bracelet is same-day/short-lead (CONANP digital or La Paz office); binding constraint is daily slot cap (~450/shift) - plan day, arrive early; book La Paz lodging on 3-6-month peak lead","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"morning Balandra slot + Playa Tecolote (vendors allowed) + Malecon afternoon; sell as half-day postcard-beach anchor of a La Paz stay year-round","holiday_event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year, Semana Santa (Easter), Mexican summer holidays - domestic surges hit slot cap hardest","campaign_start_trigger":"add-on jewel, not standalone - market inside La Paz/Baja campaigns (Nov-Apr beach campaigns late summer; summer value in spring), always paired with La Paz lodging + transfer","flag":"no wildlife season; peak = weather + La Paz volume + Mexican holidays; NO lodging on-beach; hard visitor cap","sources":["https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/balandra-beach-mexico/","https://beachythings.site/playa-balandra-entrance-fee-rules/","https://mrplayas.com/la-paz/beaches"]},"jewels":[{"name":"El Hongo mushroom-rock walk + swim","si_tag":"tropical","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"beach-day tour/transfer + CONANP bracelet or self-drive","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puerto_Balandra,_Baja_California_Sur","hook":"wade the shallow flats to Baja''s most-photographed rock, the emblem of La Paz","si":"tropical","blurb":"wade the shallow flats to Baja''s most-photographed rock, the emblem of La Paz","commission":"DMC transfer + Viator/GYG affiliate"},{"name":"Kayak / SUP the turquoise flats","si_tag":"tropical","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable":"local kayak/SUP rental/tour","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/balandra-beach-mexico/","hook":"paddle glass-calm, waist-deep water around the coves; low-impact, all-ages","si":"tropical","blurb":"paddle glass-calm, waist-deep water around the coves; low-impact, all-ages","commission":"operator + GYG affiliate"},{"name":"Shallow-water kids'' beach day","si_tag":"family","status":"future","tier":"essential","bookable":"beach-day transfer + bracelet","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/balandra-beach-mexico/","hook":"near-waveless, waist-deep flats — one of Baja''s safest child-friendly swims","si":"family","blurb":"near-waveless, waist-deep flats — one of Baja''s safest child-friendly swims","commission":"DMC transfer + affiliate"},{"name":"Balandra + Tecolote combo day","si_tag":"family","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable":"combined beach-day tour","source":"https://mrplayas.com/la-paz/beaches","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"pair protected Balandra with nearby Playa Tecolote for a full family beach day","si":"family","blurb":"pair protected Balandra with nearby Playa Tecolote for a full family beach day","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"local operator + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Sunrise/early-slot photo morning","si_tag":"romance","status":"future","tier":"premier","bookable":"private driver-guide + bracelet","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/balandra-beach-mexico/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"postcard turquoise + El Hongo before the crowds and heat — couples'' shoot backdrop","si":"romance","blurb":"postcard turquoise + El Hongo before the crowds and heat — couples'' shoot backdrop","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"Journey Mexico/Amstar DMC + affiliate"}],"faq":[{"q":"How do I get into Balandra, and what does it cost?","a":"Arrive at least 30 minutes before your shift and buy a conservation bracelet — Balandra is not a walk-up-anytime beach. Entry runs in two fixed daily slots (08:00–12:00, 13:00–17:00), capped near 450 visitors each on a first-come basis, with a ~MXN 125 pp/day CONANP bracelet (exemptions for under-12s, seniors and people with disabilities).","source":"thoroughlytravel.com","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"When is the best time for photos at El Hongo?","a":"Take the 08:00 morning slot in the cooler Nov–Apr months for the best light and the emptiest sand. Balandra fills its ~450-per-slot cap fastest in peak season and over Mexican holidays, and midday desert glare flattens the turquoise — so the early shift gives couples both the calm water and the postcard color.","source":"thoroughlytravel.com","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Balandra?","a":"Sun, heat and the lack of services — not crime. There is scarce shade, no food or water vendors and no lifeguards inside the bay, and hurricane season runs Jun–Nov; bring an umbrella, hydration and reef-safe sunscreen, and carry trip insurance for summer/fall dates.","source":"dossier","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Balandra Beach La Paz: El Hongo & Entry Rules 2026","meta_description":"Wade the shallow turquoise flats of protected Playa Balandra to El Hongo mushroom rock — timed entry (~450/slot), conservation bracelet, no services. Plan the day.","slug":"balandra-beach-mexico","primary_keyword":"Balandra beach La Paz","long_tail":["Balandra beach entrance fee 2026","Playa Balandra timed entry rules","El Hongo mushroom rock La Paz","Balandra vs Tecolote beach","Balandra shallow water family beach"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["Playa Balandra La Paz horarios","brazalete Balandra CONANP precio","El Hongo de Balandra","playa protegida La Paz aguas someras","Balandra vs Tecolote","Playa Balandra niños familia","cómo llegar a Balandra La Paz"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":{"bin":"freely_bookable","level":"L2","codes":[],"note":"Quintana Roo/Mexico US L2 (Exercise Increased Caution) - freely bookable; MXN currency, USD widely accepted"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-31","hits":3,"misses":19,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"tropical","name":"tropical","status":"live","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW"},{"si":"family","name":"family","status":"future","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"future","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Private driver-guide Balandra morning (from La Paz/Los Cabos luxury base)","posture":"no on-beach lodging exists; ultra play is private guide + early-slot + provisioning","price_tier":"luxury","earning":"on application via host / Journey Mexico DMC","virtuoso_value_add":"private guide + chilled provisioning (no vendors) + pairing with Espiritu Santo","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/balandra-beach-mexico/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Balandra Beach (Playa Balandra), Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":24.32,"lng":-110.33}}'::jsonb, 8),
  ('banos-ecuador', '10S', 'Baños de Agua Santa, Ecuador', 'Ecuador', 'Baños de Agua Santa', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Andes (Quito) & Galápagos', '{"wellness","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","luxury"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_note":"Mainland L4 (Do Not Travel): Esmeraldas city/north, Guayaquil south of Portete de Tarqui Ave, Durán canton, Huaquillas/Arenillas. Baños/Tungurahua province not named in any L3/L4 zone.","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","air_access_verified":"No airport in Baños — access via UIO (Mariscal Sucre, Quito) + ~3-3.5 hr road transfer (~180 km)","altitude_m":1820,"altitude_notes":{"banos_m":1820,"casa_del_arbol_runtun_m":2600,"mild_ams":"uncommon at town level (1,820m); watch if arriving from Quito 2,850m or higher paramo; exertion at 2,600m viewpoints is real work","trauma":"Local hospital for stabilization; serious trauma routes to Ambato (~40 min) then Quito (~3-3.5 hr); complex cases evac to US (Miami)"},"volcano":{"name":"Tungurahua","type":"active stratovolcano (~5,023m)","status_2026":"background / very-low IG-EPN alert; no eruption activity; 24/7 monitoring; UNESCO Geopark (2025)","history":"near-continuous eruption 1999-2016, quiet since 2016","rule":"Re-verify live IG-EPN status before each booking; know town ashfall/lahar evacuation routes","monitoring_source":"https://www.igepn.edu.ec/tungurahua"},"water":"not reliably potable — bottled/filtered (distinct from thermal-bath waters, for soaking not drinking)","advisory_source":"https://travel.state.gov/en/international-travel/travel-advisories/ecuador.html (Level 2)","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Coastal Region FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region provinces of: Esmeraldas Manabí Santa Elena Guayas El Oro Los Ríos Santo Domingo de los Tsáchilas This does not apply to airside transit within Guayaquil Airport in Guayas province."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border, except for these areas in Carchi province: El Ángel Ecological Reserve Rumichaca border crossing the town of Tulcán the Pan-American Highway Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to Guayaquil, except for airside transit through the airport."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to those provinces) and get local advice on where to visit."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region provinces of: Esmeraldas Manabi Santa Elena El Oro Los Ríos Santo Domingo de los Tsáchilas This is due to a high level of gang-related violence linked to the presence of organised crime relating to the production and trafficking of illegal drugs."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region province of Guayas, except: airside transit within Guayaquil Airport in Guayas province."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border, except for these areas in Carchi province: El Ángel Ecological Reserve Rumichaca border crossing the town of Tulcán the Pan-American Highway This is due to the presence of organised crime linked to the production and trafficking of drugs."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-10T10:44:44+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":["Sep","Oct","Nov","Dec","Jan","Feb"],"shoulder_green":["Mar","Apr","May","Jun","Jul","Aug"],"inflection":["Aug","Feb","Mar"],"fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks (mid-Aug for the Sep-Feb dry peak; 1-2 weeks ahead of Ecuadorian holiday weekends/Carnaval/Semana Santa); fire against the arriving Quito curve when Baños rides as an Andes/Amazon attach","events":["Ecuadorian national holiday weekends (feriados) — domestic-demand spikes","Carnaval (Feb-Mar)","Semana Santa"],"rafting_note":"Pastaza Class III+ year-round; Class IV seasonal (~Aug-May)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Casa del Árbol — Swing at the End of the World","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/Banos-attractions/Casa-del-Arbol-Swing/d22150-a19710","timing":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the iconic treehouse swing on the Runtún ridge, launching out over the Tungurahua gorge; entry ~$1, 07:00–19:00, harness-secured, 18+","si":"expedition","blurb":"the iconic treehouse swing on the Runtún ridge, launching out over the Tungurahua gorge; entry ~$1, 07:00–19:00, harness-secured, 18+","when":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","commission":"Guided swing/viewpoint tour affiliate or DMC leg (entry non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Pailón del Diablo (Devil''s Cauldron waterfall)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.zoegoesplaces.com/cascada-el-pailon-del-diablo-ecuador/","timing":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"is one of Ecuador''s most dramatic waterfalls — roughly 80 m tall with a plunge pool ~20 m deep","si":"expedition","blurb":"is one of Ecuador''s most dramatic waterfalls — roughly 80 m tall with a plunge pool ~20 m deep","when":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","commission":"Ruta de las Cascadas day-trip affiliate/DMC (trail entry non-comm.)"},{"name":"Ruta de las Cascadas (bike / chiva)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://southamericabackpacker.com/ruta-de-las-cascadas-banos/","hook":"~16 km of seven waterfalls downhill from Baños along the Pastaza","si":"expedition","blurb":"~16 km of seven waterfalls downhill from Baños along the Pastaza","commission":"Bike-hire + guided-route/chiva-tour affiliate (fall/cable fees non-comm.)"},{"name":"Canyoning — Río Blanco","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.geotoursbanios.com/","timing":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","commission":"Local adventure-operator booking (Geotours/Ivagatours) — guided-only"},{"name":"Whitewater rafting — Río Pastaza (Class III-IV)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/Banos-tours/White-Water-Rafting/d22150-g17-c27534","timing":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"half-day guided runs; Class III+ year-round, Class IV seasonal; PFD + helmet + river guide","si":"expedition","blurb":"half-day guided runs; Class III+ year-round, Class IV seasonal; PFD + helmet + river guide","when":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","commission":"Local operator + activity affiliate"},{"name":"Mirador Bellavista","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.ecuatouring.com/banos-travel-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"a short, steep hike for the postcard panorama of Baños in its gorge with Tungurahua behind — a free, romantic sunset jewel","si":"expedition","blurb":"a short, steep hike for the postcard panorama of Baños in its gorge with Tungurahua behind — a free, romantic sunset jewel","when":"year-round","commission":"Guided town-and-viewpoint walk affiliate or self-guided add-on"},{"name":"Termas de la Virgen thermal baths (at night)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g312857-d20120113-Reviews-Termas_de_la_Virgen-Banos_Tungurahua_Province.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"soak in Tungurahua-heated, sulfate-rich mineral pools in the town center, beneath the floodlit Cabellera de la Virgen waterfall; open into the evening, ~$4 entry","si":"romance","blurb":"soak in Tungurahua-heated, sulfate-rich mineral pools in the town center, beneath the floodlit Cabellera de la Virgen waterfall; open into the evening, ~$4 entry","when":"year-round","commission":"Entry non-commissionable — monetize spa-hotel room-night + private spa add-on"},{"name":"Luna Volcán / former Luna Runtún — spa with volcano view","si_tag":"romance","tier":"luxury","source":"https://www.booking.com/hotel/ec/luna-volcan-adventure-spa.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"perched on Tungurahua''s flank on 35 ha of Andean forest, infinity pool over the valley, themed suites; the marquee romantic-adventure perch above Baños","si":"romance","blurb":"perched on Tungurahua''s flank on 35 ha of Andean forest, infinity pool over the valley, themed suites; the marquee romantic-adventure perch above Baños","when":"year-round","commission":"Direct/luxury-specialist + bedbank; property/wing buyout for weddings"},{"name":"Samari Spa Resort (converted monastery)","si_tag":"wellness","tier":"luxury","source":"https://www.luxurylatinamerica.com/ecuador/samari.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"wellness","when":"year-round","commission":"Direct/luxury-specialist + bedbank — future Wellness SI anchor"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is the \"Swing at the End of the World\" worth it — and how much?","a":"Yes, and it is cheap — it is the image that put Baños on a million screens. The Casa del Árbol treehouse swing launches you out over the Tungurahua gorge from the Runtún ridge at ~2,600 m; the complex opens 07:00–19:00, entry is ~$1, and staff clip you into a climbing harness on a steel-beam frame.","source":"viator.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where can couples soak in thermal baths at night in Baños?","a":"At the Termas de la Virgen, in the town center beneath the floodlit Cabellera de la Virgen waterfall. Its sulfate-rich pools are heated by Tungurahua, open 05:00–17:00 and again 18:00–22:00, at ~$4 adult entry — the signature romantic-and-restorative Baños ritual, best paired with a volcano-view spa-hotel room-night.","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Is Baños a genuine wellness and spa destination?","a":"Increasingly, yes — the town''s name literally means \"Baths of Holy Water.\" The anchor is Samari Spa Resort, a 300-year-old former Jesuit monastery on ~10 acres with a heated indoor pool, sauna, Turkish bath, whirlpool and full spa, ranked among Baños''s top hotels — mineral-rich thermal springs fed by Tungurahua''s volcanic heat make Baños a natural wellness base.","source":"luxurylatinamerica.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"wellness-—-future-si"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Baños?","a":"Not urban crime — the load-bearing risk is activity risk. ~88% of Ecuador''s homicides occur in five coastal provinces, and the Andean highlands including Baños run below the homicide rates of many mid-sized US cities; the town''s core product is adrenaline (canyoning, Class III–IV rafting, the swing, highway cycling), so guided-vs-unguided is the whole game.","source":"myecuadorvisa.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the Tungurahua volcano dangerous right now?","a":"It is a real, live geohazard held quiet by monitoring — not a decorative caveat. Tungurahua erupted near-continuously 1999–2016, then went quiet; as of mid-2026 IG-EPN reports background/very-low activity with no precursor signals and 24/7 instrument monitoring, so any escalation would trigger alerts well in advance. Re-verify live IG-EPN status before booking.","source":"igepn.edu.ec, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is canyoning or the swing in Baños dangerous?","a":"Both carry real, activity-specific risk that guiding and gear mitigate. Canyoning on the Río Blanco is a guided-only roped waterfall-descent sport (helmet, harness, wetsuit, certified guide); the Casa del Árbol swing is 18+ with a ~220 lb (100 kg) weight limit and requires the operator''s climbing harness every ride. Never freelance either — book reputable operators like Geotours or Ivagatours.","source":"geotoursbanios.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Baños de Agua Santa, Ecuador — The Swing, Waterfalls, Rafting & Thermal Baths | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-EC","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Baños Ecuador","Casa del Árbol columpio","columpio fin del mundo Baños","Pailón del Diablo","Ruta de las Cascadas","rafting río Pastaza Baños","canyoning Baños","Termas de la Virgen","volcán Tungurahua estado","hoteles con spa en Baños"],"hreflang":["en","es-EC"],"primary_keyword":"Baños de Agua Santa"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"wellness","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Luna Volcán, Adventure SPA (formerly Luna Runtún)","category":"Boutique adventure-spa on Tungurahua''s flank, 30 rooms, 35-ha forest","mor":"Luxury-specialist / direct trade + bedbank; Fora/host-agency on direct","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Samari Spa Resort","category":"300-yr converted-monastery spa resort, ~10 acres","mor":"Luxury-specialist / direct trade + bedbank; host-agency/Fora on direct","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Casa del Suizo","category":"Amazon-edge Napo River jungle lodge (Ahuano), 75 rooms","mor":"DMC package / luxury-specialist — the Amazon-extend upsell","tier":"$$$-$$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Baños de Agua Santa, Ecuador, Ecuador"},"geo":{"lat":-1.3928,"lng":-78.4269}}'::jsonb, 9),
  ('blue-hole-belize', '10S', 'The Belize Atolls & Blue Hole', 'Belize', 'Atolls, walls and the Blue Hole', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Belize', '{"liveaboard","expedition","tropical"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Great Blue Hole is 318 m (1,043 ft) across and 124 m (407 ft) deep, near the center of Lighthouse Reef ~70 km (43 mi) off Belize City.","Belize has three coral atolls — Turneffe, Lighthouse Reef, Glover''s Reef — within the UNESCO-listed Belize Barrier Reef Reserve System.","Blue Hole stalactites hang at ~100-140 ft (30-42 m); the dive reaches ~40 m/130 ft with a narrow no-deco window — Advanced cert recommended.","Belize Aggressor III/IV depart Belize City Saturdays, up to 5 dives/day, 24-27 dives on a 7-night charter (39-42 on 10-night).","Whale sharks gather at Gladden Spit (southern Belize) around the full moon March-June."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","marine_vhf":"Channel 16","hyperbaric_chamber":"Belize Chamber Project Ltd, San Pedro (Ambergris Caye) — only DAN-Preferred chamber in Belize, 24/7; hours of boat+air transit from the offshore atolls","advisory_date":"2026-06-18","advisory_codes":"C (Crime) only","book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":true,"state_dept_carveout":"only Southside Belize City restricted; offshore atolls open","stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":true,"no_fly_after_diving":"12h single no-deco dive / 18h multi-day repetitive / 24h recommended buffer before BZE flight home","water":"open Caribbean ocean; no malaria offshore; high sun/sea exposure; DAN dive insurance with evac coverage effectively mandatory"},"timing":{"type":"dive-calendar","dive_calendar":true,"curve_start":"2026-02-15","peak":"March-June (Blue Hole best flat seas April-June)","whale_shark_window":["2026-03-14","2026-04-13","2026-05-12","2026-06-11"],"booking_lead_months":"4-6 (peak charters / full-boat buyouts longer)","shoulder_green_season":"September-November (wet/rougher, off-season fill)","fire_date":"2026-02-01","trigger_date":"2026-02-01","sharpen_note":"sharpen on live tracking — Aggressor charter availability + whale-shark sighting logs; flat-sea onset shifts yearly"},"jewels":[{"name":"The Great Blue Hole (Lighthouse Reef)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"premier","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Blue_Hole","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"A near-perfect flooded karst sinkhole near the center of Lighthouse Reef, roughly 70 km off Belize City","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","blurb":"A near-perfect flooded karst sinkhole near the center of Lighthouse Reef, roughly 70 km off Belize City","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane (Aggressor)"},{"name":"Half Moon Caye Wall + Natural Monument","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/Tropical Islands","tier":"premier","source":"https://ambergriscaye.com/pages/town/divelighthouse.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"is rated by many divers as the single best dive site in Belize","si":"Dive Liveaboards/Tropical Islands","blurb":"is rated by many divers as the single best dive site in Belize","when":"year-round","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane; park fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"The Painted Wall & Quebrada (Lighthouse Reef)","si_tag":"liveaboard","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/kbyg_document/Belize","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane"},{"name":"Turneffe Elbow (Turneffe Atoll)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.divessi.com/en/mydiveguide/divesite/98293","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane or Fora via Turneffe resorts"},{"name":"Glover''s Reef (remote atoll)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.belizeadventure.ca/atolls-of-belize/","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane (scarcity — few boats reach it)"},{"name":"Gladden Spit whale sharks (seasonal, southern Belize)","si_tag":"GEA/Dive Liveaboards","tier":"comfort","source":"https://belizescuba.com/diving-snorkeling/whale-sharks/","si":"GEA/Dive Liveaboards","commission":"AFF/day-operator or Fora via Placencia; marine-reserve fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"Tobacco Caye","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.belizeadventure.ca/atolls-of-belize/","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"March-June","commission":"Fora lane (small guesthouse packages)"},{"name":"Long Caye (Lighthouse Reef)","si_tag":"Tropical Islands/Dive Liveaboards","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.belizehighcommission.com/areas-of-belize/lighthouse-reef-bz","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Tropical Islands/Dive Liveaboards","when":"March-June","commission":"Fora / own-CLIA depending on operator"}],"faq":[{"q":"How many dives do you get on a Belize Aggressor liveaboard trip?","a":"Up to five dives a day — 24–27 dives on a 7-night charter, 39–42 on a 10-night. The Aggressor III/IV depart the Fort George dock in Belize City every Saturday at 6 pm, dive Sunday morning to Friday noon, and reach all three atolls, so the liveaboard converts a long day-boat run into unlimited access to Lighthouse Reef, Turneffe and Glover''s.","source":"aggressor.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"How deep is the Great Blue Hole dive and do you need to be certified?","a":"The dive reaches ~40 m/130 ft — at or beyond the recreational limit — to see the stalactites that hang between roughly 100–140 ft. Bottom time is measured in minutes and nitrogen narcosis is a real factor, so reputable operators strongly recommend or require Advanced Open Water certification. It is a deliberately deep dive, not a beginner novelty.","source":"dive-the-world.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What is there to do on the Belize atolls if you don''t dive?","a":"The atoll cayes carry barefoot reef-island character for surface-interval and non-diver days. Tobacco Caye is a few-acre reef caye with snorkel-off-the-dock access; Half Moon Caye is a natural monument with ~4,000 nesting red-footed boobies and an observation tower; Long Caye is the inhabited base camp for Blue Hole and Half Moon Caye dives.","source":"belizeadventure.ca, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for on an atoll dive trip?","a":"Offshore remoteness from the chamber. The only DAN-Preferred recompression chamber in Belize is on San Pedro, Ambergris Caye — hours of boat-then-air transit from a hit at Lighthouse Reef (~70 km/43 mi offshore) or Glover''s. Liveaboards carry onboard O2 and run DAN protocols as first response, which is why depth and deco discipline are non-negotiable and DAN insurance with evacuation coverage is effectively mandatory.","source":"ambergriscaye.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How long do you have to wait to fly after diving the Blue Hole?","a":"Plan an 18–24 hour buffer. DAN guidance sets a minimum 12-hour surface interval after a single no-deco dive and a minimum 18 hours after multi-day repetitive diving, which every liveaboard trip is; 24 hours is the recommended general practice. A 7-night Aggressor charter ends diving Friday around noon for a Saturday departure precisely to give that buffer before the BZE flight home.","source":"dan.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Great Blue Hole & Belize Atolls Diving — Liveaboard, Lighthouse Reef, Turneffe & Glover''s | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Belize Blue Hole liveaboard","diving Lighthouse Reef Belize","Belize Aggressor","Great Blue Hole dive depth","Turneffe Atoll diving","Glover''s Reef liveaboard","Half Moon Caye Wall dive","Belize whale shark diving Gladden Spit","no fly after diving Belize"],"hreflang":["en"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["liveaboard","expedition","tropical"],"ultra":[{"name":"Private full-boat liveaboard charter (Belize Aggressor III/IV buyout)","tier":"ultra","mor":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane — convertible affiliate->commissioned-agent (the moat)","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/destination/belize"},{"name":"Turneffe Island Resort (luxury all-inclusive dive)","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora lane (host-agency IATA) all-inclusive dive package","source":"https://visitturneffe.org/discover/where-to-stay-on-turneffe-atoll/"},{"name":"Gladden Private Island (adjacent, southern Belize)","tier":"ultra","mor":"Fora / own-CLIA depending on channel","source":"https://www.belizeadventure.ca/atolls-of-belize/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"The Belize Atolls & Blue Hole, Belize"},"geo":{"lat":17.3158,"lng":-87.5346}}'::jsonb, 10),
  ('bocas-del-toro-panama', '10S', 'Bocas del Toro, Panama', 'Panama', 'Islands strung on a turquoise thread', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Panama', '{"tropical","diveglobal","romance","adventure"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","luxury"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_text":"Exercise Increased Caution (crime + potential civil unrest)","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","air_access_verified":true,"remote_flag":true,"hazards":["riptides (Red Frog)","advanced reef surf breaks (Bluff/Paunch)","water-taxi/boat transfers","dengue/zika/chikungunya","non-potable tap water (bottled only)"],"medical":"Bocas Town private clinic; Changuinola ~3h; Panama City evac ~11h road / short flight. Medical-evac insurance advised.","unrest_history":"State of emergency May-Jun 2025 (protests); lifted 2025-06-29; US personnel prohibition lifted 2025-07-08. Monitor before campaigns.","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/panama","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2025-12-10T13:26:25+00:00"}},"timing":{"peak_windows":["Feb-Mar (driest + best viz + surf peak)","Sep-Oct (driest secondary + low crowds)"],"surf_peak":"Dec-Mar (secondary Jun-Jul)","inflection":"late Nov -> Dec","off_season_fill":["Nov (wettest)","Apr-May","Aug"],"fire_date":["~2026-01-18 (for Feb-Mar peak)","~2026-08-20 (for Sep-Oct peak)"],"note":"Caribbean-Panama inverts the national dry season; driest = Feb-Mar and Sep-Oct."},"jewels":[{"name":"Zapatilla Cays","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","source":"https://go.bocasdeltoro.travel/destinations/cayos-zapatillas/","hook":"two uninhabited, reef-sheltered cays inside Bastimentos National Marine Park; postcard white sand + snorkeling","si":"tropical","blurb":"two uninhabited, reef-sheltered cays inside Bastimentos National Marine Park; postcard white sand + snorkeling","commission":"day-tour referral + non-commissionable park fee"},{"name":"Starfish Beach (Playa Estrella)","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","source":"https://sallysees.com/beaches-in-bocas-del-toro/","hook":"shallow, glass-clear water full of starfish on Isla Colón''s northwest tip; the archipelago''s most photographed spot","si":"tropical","blurb":"shallow, glass-clear water full of starfish on Isla Colón''s northwest tip; the archipelago''s most photographed spot","commission":"island-hop boat-tour referral"},{"name":"Red Frog Beach","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.redfrogbeach.com/about","si":"tropical","commission":"Red Frog Beach resort booking + boat transfer"},{"name":"Wizard Beach","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","source":"https://mokumsurfclub.com/ultimate-bocas-del-toro-guide/","si":"tropical","commission":"guided walk / surf-school referral"},{"name":"Cayo Coral (Coral Cay)","si_tag":"Dive/Snorkel","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.snorkeling-report.com/spot/snorkeling-cayo-coral-bocas-del-toro/","hook":"easy patch reef, 10–12 ft, mooring buoys, floating restaurants alongside. Ideal first-timer snorkel","si":"Dive/Snorkel","blurb":"easy patch reef, 10–12 ft, mooring buoys, floating restaurants alongside. Ideal first-timer snorkel","commission":"dive/snorkel operator referral"},{"name":"Bastimentos National Marine Park reefs","si_tag":"Dive/Snorkel","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.tourismpanama.com/outdoors-and-nature/nature-parks/national-parks/bastimentos-island/","si":"Dive/Snorkel","commission":"PADI operator package + park fee"},{"name":"Dolphin Bay","si_tag":"Dive/Snorkel","tier":"essential","source":"https://bocastours.com/en/packages/zapatilla-cay-tour","hook":"resident dolphin pods; combines with Zapatilla day tours","si":"Dive/Snorkel","blurb":"resident dolphin pods; combines with Zapatilla day tours","commission":"boat-tour referral (ethical operators)"},{"name":"Bioluminescence night tour","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://azoravoyages.com/customize-my-trip/panama-all-tours/bocas-del-toro-activities-tours/","hook":"2-hr boat rides across dark bays where plankton light up on movement. Pure honeymoon set-piece","si":"romance","blurb":"2-hr boat rides across dark bays where plankton light up on movement. Pure honeymoon set-piece","commission":"guided night-tour referral"},{"name":"Overwater villa nights (Nayara)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"luxury","source":"https://nayarabocasdeltoro.com/stay/","hook":"adults-only, plunge pools, glass-floor windows over the reef","si":"romance","blurb":"adults-only, plunge pools, glass-floor windows over the reef","commission":"luxury AOR / bedbank / affiliate"},{"name":"Oreba / Ngäbe cacao-farm tour","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tourismpanama.com/places-to-visit/bocas-del-toro/things-to-do/culture-and-arts/indigenous-communities/","hook":"indigenous-guided walk through a working cacao farm + artisanal chocolate. Cultural moat + weather-tolerant","si":"expedition","blurb":"indigenous-guided walk through a working cacao farm + artisanal chocolate. Cultural moat + weather-tolerant","commission":"community-tour referral"},{"name":"Bahía Honda Timorogo aquatic-trail + bat cave","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.natureretreats.org/listing/ngobe-timorogo-community-ecotourism-project/","hook":"community ecotourism boat trail into a bat cave","si":"expedition","blurb":"community ecotourism boat trail into a bat cave","commission":"community-tour referral"},{"name":"Surf the Bluff / Paunch / Wizard","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://mokumsurfclub.com/ultimate-bocas-del-toro-guide/","hook":"Sharp split by ability: Bluff and Paunch are advanced reef breaks; Wizard is beginner-friendly when small and used by surf schools","si":"expedition","blurb":"Sharp split by ability: Bluff and Paunch are advanced reef breaks; Wizard is beginner-friendly when small and used by surf schools","commission":"surf-school / lesson referral"},{"name":"Bocas Town Caribbean nightlife","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.takeyourbackpack.com/backpacking-in-panama/visit-bocas-del-toro/","hook":"the stilted harbor town''s bars, over-water clubs, and reggae/soca scene","si":"expedition","blurb":"the stilted harbor town''s bars, over-water clubs, and reggae/soca scene","commission":"F&B / experience add-on (drives room-nights)"}],"faq":null,"seo":{"meta_title":"Bocas del Toro, Panama Travel Guide 2026 — Islands, Reefs, Overwater Villas | TravelWell","search_language":"es-PA","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","freshness":"2026-07-07","local_keywords":["Bocas del Toro qué hacer","Cayos Zapatillas","Isla Bastimentos","Bocas del Toro cuándo ir","playa Estrella Bocas","surf en Bocas del Toro","tour bioluminiscencia Bocas","villas sobre el agua Panamá"],"hreflang":["en","es-PA"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Nayara Bocas del Toro","island":"Frangipani","model":"luxury-resort / Virtuoso-style preferred","tier":"luxury","mor":false,"note":"CNT #1 Central America; adults-only overwater"},{"name":"Sweet Bocas","model":"whole-estate MoR buyout","tier":"$$$$$","mor":true,"note":"AD-featured 9-BR teak overwater private-island villa; ~26 adults; $10,500/night base"},{"name":"Red Frog Beach Island Resort","island":"Bastimentos","model":"resort + villa commission","tier":"$$$","mor":"villa inventory via Red Frog Property"},{"name":"Isla Palenque","model":"luxury private-island (Pacific Gulf of Chiriquí — NOT Bocas)","tier":"luxury","mor":false,"note":"two-coast Panama add-on, not a Bocas jewel"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Bocas del Toro, Panama, Panama"},"geo":{"lat":9.3402,"lng":-82.2417}}'::jsonb, 11),
  ('bogota-colombia', '10S', 'Bogotá & The Andes, Colombia', 'Colombia', 'Andean capital, paramo on its doorstep', 'live', 'verified', 'venice', 'Bogotá & The Andes', '{"romance","adventure","culture","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Bogotá sits at ~2,640 m (8,660 ft) — one of the highest capital cities on earth; expect mild soroche (altitude effects) for 24–48 hrs on arrival.","The Gold Museum (Museo del Oro) holds ~55,000 pre-Columbian gold pieces, incl. the Muisca raft of the El Dorado legend.","Monserrate rises to 3,152 m over the city, reached by funicular, cable car or a steep daytime walk, with the Basilica at the summit.","Zipaquirá Salt Cathedral is a cathedral carved inside a working salt mine ~1.5–2 hrs from the city; Villa de Leyva has Colombia''s largest cobbled plaza (14,000 m²) and a Cretaceous fossil valley.","Bogotá''s driest, clearest windows are Dec–Mar and Jul–Aug; the biennial Ibero-American Theatre Festival returns August 2026."],"safety":{"emergency":"123","hospital":"Bogotá top private clinics (stabilization); serious cases route to US medical evacuation — evac-grade insurance advised","book_enabled":true,"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","risk_codes":["C","T","U","K","N"],"risk_code_meanings":{"C":"Crime — violent crime (murder, assault, robbery), drugging (scopolamine/''devil''s breath''), extortion, express kidnapping occur throughout Colombia incl. cities","T":"Terrorism — attacks possible with little/no warning; car bombs, grenades, IEDs, drones","U":"Unrest — demonstrations can shut roads and turn violent","K":"Kidnapping or Hostage-Taking — kidnapping-for-ransom reported","N":"Natural Disaster — earthquake, landslide (advisory names Bogotá for landslide risk)"},"named_danger":["Arauca","Cauca excl Popayán","Valle del Cauca excl Cali","Norte de Santander","Venezuela border ~10km"],"bogota_in_named_danger":false,"air_access_verified":"BOG (El Dorado Intl) — direct international incl. major US, EU and LatAm gateways; Colombia''s primary hub","altitude_m":2640,"altitude_note":"~2,640 m — mild AMS possible 24–48 hrs; Monserrate 3,152 m and páramo hikes 3,200 m+ add load","water":"Bogotá tap generally potable (meets WHO standards per EAAB/Ministry of Health); caveat aging plumbing in older buildings — bottled is conservative default","disease_note":"dengue LOW at altitude (vector scarce above ~1,800 m); rises for low-altitude excursions","scopolamine_caution":"''devil''s breath''/burundanga drugging — colourless/tasteless; Bogotá hotspot (1,409 cases 2023, Chapinero/Teusaquillo/Santa Fe); never accept drinks/food/tabs from strangers; dating-app method documented","personal_safety":"vetted taxi/ride-app only; no wealth display; zone discipline (La Candelaria daytime); do not resist a robbery"},"timing":{"peak":"Dec–Mar (dry, peak season) and Jul–Aug (dry + biennial Ibero-American Theatre Festival, even years)","inflection_curve_start":"early December (Christmas peak); August 2026 (Theatre Festival + dry season); Semana Santa (late Mar/early Apr)","fire_date":"mid-to-late November (Dec–Mar peak); ~mid-July (Aug festival/dry peak); ~early March (Semana Santa)","event_peaks":[{"event":"Ibero-American Theatre Festival","dates_2026":"August 2026 (biennial, even years)","note":"800+ productions from 40+ countries; stacks on dry season"},{"event":"Semana Santa (Holy Week)","dates":"late March / early April","note":"major domestic-travel pulse across the Andes"},{"event":"Christmas–New Year","dates":"Dec 20–Jan 6","note":"peak congestion + higher rates"}],"off_season_fill":"Apr–May and Oct–Nov (green/wetter shoulders, lower rates, thinner crowds)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Gold Museum (Museo del Oro)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/Bogota-attractions/Gold-Museum/d4560-a6188","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"~55,000 pre-Columbian gold pieces, the Muisca raft of the El Dorado legend; free on Sundays","si":"culture","blurb":"~55,000 pre-Columbian gold pieces, the Muisca raft of the El Dorado legend; free on Sundays","when":"year-round","commission":"city-tour affiliate; entry non-comm pass-through"},{"name":"Botero Museum","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://theabroadguide.com/la-candelaria-mount-monserrate-and-the-gold-museum-in-one-day-in-bogota/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Fernando Botero''s donated collection, free entry, in La Candelaria","si":"culture","blurb":"Fernando Botero''s donated collection, free entry, in La Candelaria","when":"year-round","commission":"city-tour affiliate; free entry"},{"name":"La Candelaria colonial core + street art","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://kittiaroundtheworld.com/things-to-do-in-la-candelaria-bogota-historic-centre/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Plaza de Bolívar, 17th-c. Iglesia de Santa Clara, mural-covered lanes, the number-one neighbourhood in the city","si":"culture","blurb":"Plaza de Bolívar, 17th-c. Iglesia de Santa Clara, mural-covered lanes, the number-one neighbourhood in the city","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"walking-tour affiliate + boutique lodging"},{"name":"Zipaquirá Salt Cathedral","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://thecolombianway.com/en/our-trips/day-trips/the-salt-cathedral-of-zipaquira/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"a cathedral carved inside a working salt mine, glowing tunnels, carved crosses, an underground dome; ~1.5–2 hrs from Bogotá","si":"culture","blurb":"a cathedral carved inside a working salt mine, glowing tunnels, carved crosses, an underground dome; ~1.5–2 hrs from Bogotá","when":"year-round","commission":"day-trip DMC/operator; entry non-comm pass-through"},{"name":"Villa de Leyva (colonial plaza + fossils)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"premier","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Villa_de_Leyva","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"a whitewashed-town weekend around the great plaza, star-filled Andean skies, boutique fincas — the plateau''s romance run","si":"culture","blurb":"a whitewashed-town weekend around the great plaza, star-filled Andean skies, boutique fincas — the plateau''s romance run","when":"year-round","commission":"overnight DMC + colonial-house/finca villa MoR"},{"name":"Monserrate sunset (funicular/cable car)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","source":"https://kittiaroundtheworld.com/things-to-do-in-la-candelaria-bogota-historic-centre/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"hotel + funicular non-comm + DMC dining"},{"name":"Usaquén Sunday market + brunch","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g294074-d1382992-Reviews-Mercado_de_las_Pulgas_de_Usaquen-Bogota.html","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the colonial northern district; every Sunday ~10:00–18:00 the streets fill with artisans, antiques, Colombian coffee and long brunches around the plaza","si":"romance","blurb":"the colonial northern district; every Sunday ~10:00–18:00 the streets fill with artisans, antiques, Colombian coffee and long brunches around the plaza","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"boutique-lodging + food-tour affiliate"},{"name":"Chingaza páramo hike","si_tag":"adventure","tier":"premier","source":"https://mytriptocolombia.com/hiking-chingaza-national-park-travel-guide/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a magnificent páramo on Bogotá''s outskirts, frailejón moorland, glacial Siecha/Buitrago lagoons, guided day trips from the city","si":"adventure","blurb":"a magnificent páramo on Bogotá''s outskirts, frailejón moorland, glacial Siecha/Buitrago lagoons, guided day trips from the city","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"GEA DMC / licensed guide + park permit"},{"name":"Suesca rock-climbing","si_tag":"adventure","tier":"essential","source":"https://cuppatocopatravels.com/south-america/colombia/day-trips-weekend-breaks-from-bogota-2019/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Colombia''s best climbing crag, ~1 hr north; sandstone canyon walls, beginner-to-advanced routes through local climbing schools","si":"adventure","blurb":"Colombia''s best climbing crag, ~1 hr north; sandstone canyon walls, beginner-to-advanced routes through local climbing schools","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"adventure DMC / climbing-school affiliate"},{"name":"Sumapaz páramo trek","si_tag":"adventure","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/articles/day-hikes-bogota-colombia","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the world''s largest páramo ecosystem, south of Bogotá; high-altitude moorland trekking, guided-only","si":"adventure","blurb":"the world''s largest páramo ecosystem, south of Bogotá; high-altitude moorland trekking, guided-only","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"GEA DMC / licensed guide (guided-only)"},{"name":"Paloquemao market + coffee","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","source":"https://theabroadguide.com/la-candelaria-mount-monserrate-and-the-gold-museum-in-one-day-in-bogota/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Bogotá''s great produce, flower and food market; early-morning fruit tastings and Colombian-coffee sourcing, a food-tour anchor","si":"culinary","blurb":"Bogotá''s great produce, flower and food market; early-morning fruit tastings and Colombian-coffee sourcing, a food-tour anchor","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"food-tour affiliate + DMC"},{"name":"Andrés Carne de Res (Chía)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Restaurant_Review-g815502-d939879-Reviews-Andres_Carne_De_Res_Chia-Chia_Cundinamarca_Department.html","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the legendary maximalist restaurant ~40–60 min north of Bogotá — a labyrinth of over-the-top décor, live music and improv actors","si":"culinary","blurb":"the legendary maximalist restaurant ~40–60 min north of Bogotá — a labyrinth of over-the-top décor, live music and improv actors","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"DMC dining + vetted transport"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the most romantic thing to do in Bogotá?","a":"Ride the funicular or cable car up Monserrate at dusk for dinner at the summit restaurant, with the whole plateau of light beneath you — the city''s signature romance run. The ridge rises to 3,152 m (10,341 ft), and the Basilica crowns the summit.","source":"kittiaroundtheworld.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you go hiking near Bogotá?","a":"Yes — Andean páramo day-hikes start on the city''s doorstep and run guided. Chingaza páramo climbs from 2,600 to 4,000 m through frailejón moorland and glacial Siecha/Buitrago lagoons, while Suesca, about 1 hour north, is Colombia''s premier rock-climbing crag. Guided entry is the norm for the páramos.","source":"mytriptocolombia.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"adventure"},{"q":"What are the must-see museums and sights in Bogotá?","a":"The Gold Museum (Museo del Oro) is the headline — ~55,000 pre-Columbian gold pieces, including the Muisca raft of the El Dorado legend, and free on Sundays — alongside the Botero Museum and colonial La Candelaria. The core clusters in and above the historic centre.","source":"viator.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Where should you eat and drink around Bogotá?","a":"Andrés Carne de Res in Chía is the marquee night out — ranked #2 of 139 restaurants in Chía, a labyrinth of over-the-top décor, live music and improv actors, about 40–60 min north of the city. In town, Zona G is Bogotá''s dense \"gourmet zone.\"","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Bogotá?","a":"Scopolamine (\"devil''s breath\" / burundanga) drugging is the headline traveler risk — a colourless, tasteless sedative used to rob or assault. Bogotá police recorded 1,409 cases in 2023 (+16% year-on-year), concentrated in Chapinero, Teusaquillo and Santa Fe, often via dating apps and offered drinks. Never accept drinks or tabs from strangers.","source":"thecitypaperbogota.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is walking up Monserrate dangerous?","a":"Walk the Monserrate pilgrimage trail only in daylight and in groups — robberies have been reported on the path — or take the funicular or cable car instead. The summit stands at 3,152 m, so pace yourself for the altitude.","source":"kittiaroundtheworld.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Bogotá & The Andes, Colombia — Gold Museum, Monserrate, Zipaquirá & Villa de Leyva | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-CO","long_tail_en":["things to do in Bogotá Colombia","Gold Museum Bogotá guide","Monserrate funicular Bogotá","Zipaquirá Salt Cathedral day trip from Bogotá","Villa de Leyva from Bogotá","is Bogotá safe 2026","Bogotá altitude sickness"],"local_keywords":["qué hacer en Bogotá","Catedral de Sal Zipaquirá","Museo del Oro","Villa de Leyva","Monserrate Bogotá","hoteles de lujo Bogotá"],"hreflang":["en","es-CO"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["romance","adventure","culture","culinary"],"ultra":[{"name":"Four Seasons Hotel Casa Medina","type":"landmark 1946 building, Zona G, 62 rooms + 19 suites, Ministry-of-Culture monument","routing":"Fora/Virtuoso preferred","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Four Seasons Hotel Bogotá","type":"second FS property, Zona T entertainment district, contemporary tower","routing":"Fora/Virtuoso preferred","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Sofitel Bogotá Victoria Regia","type":"French-luxury prestige address, northern corridor","routing":"preferred-partner + host","tier":"luxury→ultra"},{"name":"W Bogotá (Zona T)","type":"Marriott lifestyle-luxury flagship, design-forward rooftop","routing":"preferred-partner + host","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Click Clack Hotel","type":"design-forward boutique, northern corridor","routing":"preferred-partner + host","tier":"premium→luxury"},{"name":"Zona G / Chicó luxury-apartment buyouts","type":"serviced multi-bedroom apartments w/ concierge","routing":"MoR villa + host","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Bogotá & The Andes, Colombia, Colombia"},"geo":{"lat":4.711,"lng":-74.0721}}'::jsonb, 12),
  ('bonito-brazil', '10S', 'Bonito, Brazil', 'Brazil', 'Bonito', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Amazon, Pantanal & Iguaçu', '{"wildlife"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"190","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_why":"national crime + kidnapping risk indicator concentrated in cities, favelas, and Level-4 border zones — none describe interior Bonito","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","air_access_verified":true,"air_access":{"primary":"Bonito (BYO) — limited commercial service (~13 km from town)","gateway":"Campo Grande (CGR) + road transfer ~205 km / ~3–3.5 hrs"},"trauma_note":"rural interior; serious-trauma/evac route via Campo Grande (CGR); evacuation-coverage insurance essential for adventure stack","health_flag":"chikungunya outbreak reported in Mato Grosso do Sul — mosquito-bite prevention day and night","activity_flags":["river no-touch + no pre-entry sunscreen","cave/waterfall rappel technical + harness","cool water ~18–22°C neoprene"],"fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Amazonas State FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the following river areas towards the west of Amazonas State: along the Amazonas (Amazon) River and its tributaries west of the town of Codajás and east of the town of Belém do Solimões in Amazonas State along any part of the Itaquaí River in Amazonas State along any part of the Japurá River or its tributaries in Amazonas State along the Rio Negro (Black River) and its tributaries north or west of the town of Barcelos in Amazonas State Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel: along the Amazonas (Amazon) River and its tributaries west of the town of Codajás and east of the town of Belém do Solimões in Amazonas State along any part of the Itaquaí River in Amazonas State along any part of the Japurá River or its tributaries in Amazonas State along the Rio Negro (Black River) and its tributaries north or west of the town of Barcelos in Amazonas State There are risks to travellers in river areas towards the west of Amazonas State, where Brazil shares borders with Colombia, Peru and Venezuela, due to criminal activity."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/brazil","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-11T12:32:48+01:00"}},"timing":{"clarity_peak":"dry season ~Apr–Oct (core Jun–Sep)","crowd_price_peak":"December → Carnival","low_visibility_window":"Dec–Feb (rain raises rivers)","shoulder":"Mar–Jun (milder, fewer crowds)","inflection":"supply is physically day-capped; slots close weeks ahead in dry window","fire_date":"clarity-curve start − 1–2 weeks (late Mar–May for winter clarity trips; Oct–Nov ahead of Dec–Carnival)","off_season_fill":"dry low-season tail + wet-but-workable shoulder → flexible/budget/photography travelers","note":"attractions sell out, not just hotels — book the voucher itinerary"},"jewels":[{"name":"Rio da Prata float","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g303368-d1936985-r118728253-Rio_da_Prata-State_of_Mato_Grosso_do_Sul.html","si":"expedition","commission":"DMC/AOR → licensed-agency voucher"},{"name":"Rio Sucuri snorkel","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.aventuradobrasil.com/blog/bonito-brazils-natural-gem-of-crystal-clear-rivers-and-hidden-caves/","hook":"Described as one of the clearest rivers on Earth; emerald underwater gardens threaded with pearl-like oxygen bubbles. Gentler/shorter than Prata, superb clarity","si":"expedition","blurb":"Described as one of the clearest rivers on Earth; emerald underwater gardens threaded with pearl-like oxygen bubbles. Gentler/shorter than Prata, superb clarity","commission":"licensed-agency voucher via AOR"},{"name":"Abismo Anhumas rappel + underground-lake dive/snorkel","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.explore-share.com/trip/abismo-anhumas-abseiling-underground-lake-bonito/","hook":"72 m descent into a cavern lake with submerged limestone cones up to ~20 m; snorkel or scuba the lake; ~18°C water","si":"expedition","blurb":"72 m descent into a cavern lake with submerged limestone cones up to ~20 m; snorkel or scuba the lake; ~18°C water","commission":"AOR → operator via licensed agency"},{"name":"Boca da Onça waterfall circuit + 90m rappel","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.bocadaonca.com.br/","hook":"Mato Grosso do Sul''s tallest waterfall; Brazil''s largest platform rappel; ~4,500 m trail, 8 waterfalls, natural pools","si":"expedition","blurb":"Mato Grosso do Sul''s tallest waterfall; Brazil''s largest platform rappel; ~4,500 m trail, 8 waterfalls, natural pools","commission":"AOR → licensed-agency voucher"},{"name":"Estância Mimosa waterfall trek","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.aventuradobrasil.com/blog/bonito-brazils-natural-gem-of-crystal-clear-rivers-and-hidden-caves/","hook":"Guided trail to a chain of waterfalls and swimming pools with strong flora/fauna viewing; also offers on-site lodging","si":"expedition","blurb":"Guided trail to a chain of waterfalls and swimming pools with strong flora/fauna viewing; also offers on-site lodging","commission":"AOR → voucher + room"},{"name":"Gruta do Lago Azul","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gruta_do_Lago_Azul_Natural_Monument","hook":"Guided-mandatory, no swimming. ~300-step descent; closed-toe shoes mandatory; no water access since 1992; the risk here is the stairs, not the water","si":"expedition","blurb":"Guided-mandatory, no swimming. ~300-step descent; closed-toe shoes mandatory; no water access since 1992; the risk here is the stairs, not the water","commission":"voucher via licensed agency; entry fee pass-through"},{"name":"Buraco das Araras (macaw sinkhole)","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buraco_das_Araras_Private_Natural_Heritage_Reserve","hook":"Huge sandstone crater near Jardim; South America''s largest sinkhole; sanctuary for red-and-green macaws plus toucans/araçaris. Best at early morning / late afternoon","si":"wildlife","blurb":"Huge sandstone crater near Jardim; South America''s largest sinkhole; sanctuary for red-and-green macaws plus toucans/araçaris. Best at early morning / late afternoon","commission":"AOR → licensed reserve access"},{"name":"Night float","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.livemoretravelmore.com/things-to-do-in-bonito-brazil/","si":"wildlife","commission":"licensed-agency voucher"},{"name":"Pantanal wildlife extension (gateway)","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.aventuradobrasil.com/blog/bonito-brazils-natural-gem-of-crystal-clear-rivers-and-hidden-caves/","hook":"The high-value pairing: Bonito''s clear water + Pantanal''s unmatched wildlife density. Same regional DMC can carry both","si":"wildlife","blurb":"The high-value pairing: Bonito''s clear water + Pantanal''s unmatched wildlife density. Same regional DMC can carry both","commission":"AOR combo mandate (Bonito + Pantanal)"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to snorkel Bonito''s crystal rivers?","a":"The dry season — roughly June–September, within the broader May–September dry window — delivers the clearest, most predictable water, because the winter rains that raise rivers and drop visibility have stopped; daily visitor slots are physically capped, so book at least a week ahead in high season (July–September).","source":"lonelyplanet.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can you actually see wild macaws near Bonito?","a":"Yes — Buraco das Araras, South America''s largest sinkhole (~500 m circumference, ~100 m deep) near Jardim, is a heavily regulated sanctuary for red-and-green macaws plus toucans and araçaris, best viewed at early morning or late afternoon on a guided visit.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"Is Bonito a good honeymoon destination?","a":"Yes, as a slow water-and-forest romance add-on rather than a luxury-ceremony market: the top of the market is the 4-star Zagaia Eco Resort — grounds, pools and full recreation — with boutique eco-pousadas filling the couples tier, so set expectations to best-in-region eco, not five-star.","source":"evendo.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Is the Abismo Anhumas cave rappel dangerous?","a":"It is a serious, technical activity run safely under a guided-mandatory system: a 72 m harness rappel on electric devices into a cavern lake (~18°C water, submerged cones to ~20 m), capped at a maximum of 16 people per day with certified monitors — never a free-climb and never sold unguided.","source":"explore-share.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Bonito?","a":"Sell-outs, not danger: because every attraction runs on a licensed-agency voucher with hard daily caps, marquee tours like Rio da Prata and Rio Sucuri can sell out weeks ahead of time, so the booking *is* the reservation — reserve the voucher itinerary, not just the room.","source":"en.wikivoyage.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Bonito, Brazil: Crystal-River Snorkeling, Caves & the Pantanal Gateway — TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"pt-BR","local_keywords":["Bonito MS o que fazer","Rio da Prata flutuação","Gruta do Lago Azul","melhor época para ir a Bonito","Abismo Anhumas rapel","Boca da Onça cachoeira","Bonito e Pantanal roteiro","Buraco das Araras Jardim"],"hreflang":["en","pt-BR"],"primary_keyword":"Bonito"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"wildlife","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Zagaia Eco Resort","positioning":"4-star Bonito ceiling","earning":"room commission","mor":"DMC/AOR","tier":"Premium (regional ceiling)"},{"name":"Santa Esmeralda","positioning":"upper-boutique eco-pousada","earning":"room commission / bedbank","mor":"AOR/bedbank","tier":"Premium-lite"},{"name":"Boutique eco-pousadas (curated)","positioning":"design-forward small pousadas — premier eco ceiling, not 5-star","earning":"room commission","mor":"AOR/bedbank","tier":"Mid → Premium-lite"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Bonito, Brazil, Brazil"},"geo":{"lat":-21.1261,"lng":-56.4514}}'::jsonb, 13),
  ('buenos-aires-argentina', '10S', 'Buenos Aires, Argentina', 'Argentina', 'Leather and silk, beef and fire', 'live', 'verified', 'paris', 'Buenos Aires & The Pampas', '{"romance","culture","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["US State Dept Level 1 - Exercise Normal Precautions (advisory dated 2026-05-20); Rosario is a city-level L2 exception, not on a BA itinerary.","Best experience = spring/fall shoulder (Oct-Nov, Mar-Apr); November brings jacaranda bloom + the Argentine Open Polo.","Signature BA experiences: milonga tango, puerta-cerrada (closed-door) asado, Malbec tasting, Recoleta Cemetery (Evita), Teatro Colon.","Day-trip belt: Tigre Delta (~1 hr), San Antonio de Areco estancia (~1.5 hr), Colonia/Uruguay ferry across the Rio de la Plata.","Petty crime is theft-by-distraction, not force (motochorros, ~90% at traffic lights); La Boca daytime-and-Caminito only; tap water potable."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","police":"101","ambulance":"107","fire":"100","us_embassy_ba":"+54 11 5777-4354","advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L1)","air_access_verified":{"international":"EZE (Ezeiza / Ministro Pistarini)","domestic":"AEP (Aeroparque Jorge Newbery)"},"water":"potable","trauma_path":"BA private hospitals excellent; stabilize locally then US medevac for catastrophic cases","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/argentina","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-07T17:26:11+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak_experience":"Oct-Nov and Mar-Apr (shoulder — best weather/crowds)","peak_volume":"Dec-Feb (austral summer — hot/humid, least comfortable)","inflection_curve_start":"loads ahead of each shoulder window + Nov events","fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks (~early Sep for Oct-Nov; ~January for Mar-Apr); November premium = 3-6 months lead","events":[{"name":"Argentine Open Polo Championship","month":"November","venue":"Campo Argentino de Polo, Palermo"},{"name":"Tango BA Festival y Mundial","month":"August (austral winter — NOT November)"}],"low_season":"Jun-Aug (winter; occupancy low ~Apr-Jun — value window)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Private milonga tango night","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/buenos-aires-l1/","hook":"The real social tango — a couple''s night at an authentic milonga beats any tourist stage show for a honeymoon","si":"romance","blurb":"The real social tango — a couple''s night at an authentic milonga beats any tourist stage show for a honeymoon","commission":"activities affiliate / DMC private experience"},{"name":"Recoleta jacarandas + Recoleta Cemetery (Evita tomb)","si_tag":"RHN / Culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.buenosairesfreewalks.com/what-to-do/grave-of-evita-peron/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"A November walk through Recoleta''s lilac-blossom boulevards into the most famous cemetery in the Americas","si":"RHN / Culture","blurb":"A November walk through Recoleta''s lilac-blossom boulevards into the most famous cemetery in the Americas","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC/guide (entry non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Closed-door (puerta cerrada) asado — Fogon Asado","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/buenos-aires-l1/buenos-aires-8-course-argentine-bbq-at-fogon-asado-t235877/","hook":"The most intimate, most Porteño dinner in the city — see Culinary below; sells beautifully as a honeymoon night","si":"culinary","blurb":"The most intimate, most Porteño dinner in the city — see Culinary below; sells beautifully as a honeymoon night","commission":"activities affiliate / DMC"},{"name":"Casa Saltshaker puerta cerrada + Malbec flight","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"comfort","source":"https://theculturetrip.com/south-america/argentina/articles/the-best-closed-door-restaurants-in-buenos-aires","hook":"Intimate shared-table five-course dinners with Malbec-vs-Patagonian-pinot flights — one of the city''s oldest supper clubs","si":"culinary","blurb":"Intimate shared-table five-course dinners with Malbec-vs-Patagonian-pinot flights — one of the city''s oldest supper clubs","commission":"DMC-brokered / direct"},{"name":"Malbec / Argentine-wine tasting","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"comfort","source":"https://theculturetrip.com/south-america/argentina/articles/the-best-closed-door-restaurants-in-buenos-aires","hook":"Guided verticals of Mendoza Malbec, Patagonian pinot, and high-altitude Salta torrontés — in-city tasting rooms or a DMC-curated flight","si":"culinary","blurb":"Guided verticals of Mendoza Malbec, Patagonian pinot, and high-altitude Salta torrontés — in-city tasting rooms or a DMC-curated flight","commission":"DMC / activities affiliate"},{"name":"San Telmo Sunday feria (Calle Defensa)","si_tag":"Culinary / Culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Buenos_Aires","hook":"The Sunday street market and antiques fair — empanadas, choripán, street tango, and browsing","si":"Culinary / Culture","blurb":"The Sunday street market and antiques fair — empanadas, choripán, street tango, and browsing","commission":"content-led; guided-tour affiliate"},{"name":"MALBA — Latin American art museum","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Buenos_Aires/Palermo_%26_Recoleta","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"admission non-commissionable; DMC guided visit"},{"name":"Teatro Colon guided tour / opera night","si_tag":"Culture / RHN","tier":"essential","source":"https://turismo.buenosaires.gob.ar/en","si":"Culture / RHN","commission":"box-office non-commissionable; DMC package"},{"name":"Palermo Soho boutiques","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Buenos_Aires/Palermo_%26_Recoleta","hook":"High-end Argentine fashion and leather boutiques on cobblestone streets — the \"silk\" half of BA''s soul","si":"culture","blurb":"High-end Argentine fashion and leather boutiques on cobblestone streets — the \"silk\" half of BA''s soul","commission":"content-led; concierge personal-shopper"},{"name":"La Boca / Caminito (daytime only)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://solsalute.com/blog/is-buenos-aires-safe-for-tourists/","hook":"The painted tin tenements, birthplace of tango and of Boca Juniors — a guided daytime visit only","si":"culture","blurb":"The painted tin tenements, birthplace of tango and of Boca Juniors — a guided daytime visit only","commission":"guided-tour affiliate / DMC"},{"name":"Tigre Delta day","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://luxurylatinamerica.com/blog/2023/03/13/day-trips-from-buenos-aires/","hook":"An hour north, the Paraná Delta''s maze of channels and stilt-houses","si":"culture","blurb":"An hour north, the Paraná Delta''s maze of channels and stilt-houses","commission":"activities affiliate / DMC day-tour"},{"name":"Pampas estancia day — San Antonio de Areco (gaucho)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://solsalute.com/blog/best-buenos-aires-day-trips/","hook":"~1½ hrs out onto the grasslands to a working ranch: horseback, all-afternoon asado, folklore, and gaucho tradition","si":"culture","blurb":"~1½ hrs out onto the grasslands to a working ranch: horseback, all-afternoon asado, folklore, and gaucho tradition","commission":"DMC / MoR estancia booking"},{"name":"Argentine Open Polo (November, Palermo)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.theaircharterjournal.com/air-charter-journal/argentine-polo-open-2025","hook":"The world''s most prestigious polo championship, at the \"Cathedral of Polo\" — grandstand and hospitality seats are a marquee November draw","si":"culture","blurb":"The world''s most prestigious polo championship, at the \"Cathedral of Polo\" — grandstand and hospitality seats are a marquee November draw","commission":"DMC / hospitality-package MoR"},{"name":"Colonia del Sacramento day trip (Uruguay)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://luxurylatinamerica.com/blog/2023/03/13/day-trips-from-buenos-aires/","hook":"Ferry across the Río de la Plata to a UNESCO colonial town — the calm counterpoint to BA","si":"culture","blurb":"Ferry across the Río de la Plata to a UNESCO colonial town — the calm counterpoint to BA","commission":"ferry affiliate + DMC day-tour"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to visit Buenos Aires for a honeymoon?","a":"The spring and fall shoulders — October–November and March–April — are the sweet spot, with mild 18–26 °C days and thinner crowds than the hot, humid summer. November is the standout: the jacarandas bloom lilac across Recoleta''s boulevards and the Argentine Open Polo fills Palermo, so treat November premium beds as a 3–6 month advance book.","source":"lonelyplanet.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What are the must-see cultural sites in Buenos Aires?","a":"Start with Recoleta Cemetery — 6,400+ statues and crypts, including Evita Perón''s tomb, with free Spanish guided tours Tue–Sun — then Teatro Colón, one of the great opera houses of the world, and a daytime visit to La Boca''s Caminito, birthplace of tango. San Telmo''s Sunday feria on Calle Defensa rounds out the heritage circuit.","source":"buenosairesfreewalks.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What is a puerta cerrada (closed-door) restaurant?","a":"They are secret chef''s-home supper clubs, a Porteño institution. Fogón Asado runs a Michelin-recommended 9-course asado tasting for ~35 guests with optional Argentine wine pairings, while Casa Saltshaker (est. 2005) does intimate shared-table five-course dinners with Malbec-vs-Patagonian-pinot flights — one of the city''s oldest such houses.","source":"theculturetrip.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Buenos Aires?","a":"Snatch-and-grab theft, not violence. BA''s characteristic street crime is motochorros (motorcycle thieves) and distraction scams, with roughly 90% of motochorro snatchings happening at traffic lights; keep your phone off café-table edges and use vetted radio-taxi or ride-apps. La Boca is daytime-and-Caminito only — arrive by taxi and leave before dark.","source":"secretsofbuenosaires.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Do I need travel insurance for Argentina?","a":"Treat it as required and always buy it. Under Decree 366/2025, effective 2025-07-01, non-resident travelers were required to carry travel medical insurance covering emergency care, hospitalization, evacuation and repatriation, with airlines confirming at check-in. One December-2025 secondary source reported the rule may have been suspended or modified (unverified and conflicting), so verify current enforcement at booking.","source":"globalrescue.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Buenos Aires Travel Guide — Tango, Steak & Boutique Hotels | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-AR","long_tail_en":["things to do in Buenos Aires","best tango show Buenos Aires","closed-door restaurants Buenos Aires","Buenos Aires honeymoon","best time to visit Buenos Aires","Recoleta cemetery Evita","Tigre Delta day trip","San Antonio de Areco estancia","Buenos Aires luxury hotels","is Buenos Aires safe"],"local_keywords":["qué hacer en Buenos Aires","show de tango Buenos Aires","mejores parrillas Buenos Aires","puertas cerradas Buenos Aires","Cementerio de la Recoleta Evita","estancia San Antonio de Areco","escapada al Delta del Tigre","hoteles de lujo Buenos Aires","Abierto Argentino de Polo","mejor época para visitar Buenos Aires"],"hreflang":["en","es-AR"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Four Seasons Hotel Buenos Aires + La Mansion","barrio":"Recoleta","tier":"ultra","earning":"FS Preferred Partner / Virtuoso — commission + amenities (UNVERIFIED %)"},{"name":"Alvear Palace Hotel","barrio":"Recoleta","tier":"ultra","earning":"Virtuoso / LHW — commission + amenities (UNVERIFIED %)"},{"name":"Palacio Duhau — Park Hyatt Buenos Aires","barrio":"Recoleta","tier":"ultra","earning":"Hyatt Prive / Virtuoso — commission + amenities (UNVERIFIED %)"},{"name":"Faena Hotel Buenos Aires","barrio":"Puerto Madero","tier":"ultra","earning":"Virtuoso / brand luxury — commission + amenities (UNVERIFIED %)"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Buenos Aires, Argentina, Argentina"},"geo":{"lat":-34.6037,"lng":-58.3816}}'::jsonb, 14)
